    "Generation: produce initial synthetic "goldens" that serve as raw QA inputs and starting, automatically created questions and answers.",
    "Filtration: remove low-quality or unsafe goldens so that only good candidates remain.",
    "Filtration uses a critique model (an evaluator LLM) and a threshold, with a default of 0.5 and an example of 0.6.",
    "The filtration step removes bad questions that you would not give to the LLM or that do not meet generation standards.",
    "Evolution: rewrite the filtered goldens to make them more complex and realistic.",
    "An LLM rewrites each filtered item, often repeated num_evolution times, so the synthetic QA looks closer to human-curated goldens.",
    "The goal of evolution is to make the data more realistic, richer, and harder to distinguish from real data.",
    "The target is to approach about 80–90% of human quality.",
    "Styling defines the output format for the evolved inputs and their answers.",
    "Styling makes the QA pairs consistent, realistic, and usable for downstream tests or models.",
    "Styling is set in the evolution config as a set.",
    "The final synthetic goldens should match expected formats and look like real-world examples."
] 

